# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OMSI 2 content must never be committed.
#
# This project reads a game installation to test its parsers. Nothing from one may end up
# here: the formats are not ours, the content is not licensed for redistribution, and a
# stray .bus or .dds would put someone's copy of a commercial game into a public
# repository. The tests build synthetic content in a temporary folder instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bus
*.ovh
*.tram
*.zug
*.ttf        # TrueType in an install; NOT an OMSI timetable (those are .ttp/.ttl/.ttr)
*.oft
*.ttp
*.ttl
*.ttr
*.hof
*.dds
*.o3d
*.x
*.surf
*.trd
*.map
*.scenery
*.psd
*.pdn
*.blend
*.blend1
*.skb
*.cpt
*.dtm
*.prt
*.otf
*.envir

# Archives that may hold mod content
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z

# The hold folder a clean writes to. Its whole purpose is to sit outside the
# repository, but a stray --move-to . would otherwise land here.
omsi-clean/
quarantine/
evigit-clean/